# tokopedia-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy this file to `.env` next to the scripts and fill in what you use:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is in .gitignore. Keep it there. A secret passed on a command line
# is readable by anything that can run `ps` and lands in your shell history,
# which is why none of these has a flag you are expected to type.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#
#     explicit CLI flag  >  exported environment variable  >  .env  >  default
#
# So a `.env` never overrides something you typed, and an already-exported
# variable (a CI secret, direnv, your shell profile) is never clobbered by a
# file you forgot to delete.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing any secret:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# Every variable below is one this code actually reads, and every variable
# the code reads is below — smoke_test.py asserts the two sets are equal in
# both directions, because a documented-but-unread variable is worse than an
# undocumented one.


# --- 2Captcha -------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. https://2captcha.com
#
# WORTH KNOWING BEFORE YOU BUY SOLVING FOR THIS SITE: it buys nothing here.
# No challenge of any kind has been observed on Tokopedia — measured
# 2026-09-10 across six live captures — and a refusal is not a page at all:
# the connection is accepted, TLS completes, the HTTP/2 stream opens, and
# then it is reset. There is no captcha to solve, no interstitial, not even a
# status code. What clears a refusal is a residential exit.
#
# The solving path is wired up and capped at one purchase per page, because a
# bot manager can be switched on between deploys and a scraper that cannot
# name what stopped it is much harder to fix. It is not part of the happy
# path.
#
# This key IS what --fingerprint uses (a separate subscription from solving:
# a working solver key is not automatically enabled for fingerprints, and the
# client says so by name if it is not).
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# --- Scraping Browser API -------------------------------------------------
# A remote browser you do not run or patch, with a persistent profile and a
# chosen exit country. Used by --cdp-endpoint, and on this site it is the
# path that works.
#
#   country-  picks the exit country. On this site that decides whether you
#             get IN and NOTHING about what comes back: an Indonesian exit
#             (country-id) and a US one (country-us) returned identical
#             markup, identical `<html lang="id">`, identical IDR prices and
#             ZERO price differences across the 68 products both runs saw.
#             Tokopedia has one storefront and does not geo-redirect, so
#             there is no --country flag on the scrapers either.
#   pid-      is a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each,
#             capped per account — reuse pids rather than minting one per
#             run, and expect a 500 (`profile_locked`, exit 5) while another
#             run still holds this one. Measured: two runs launched back to
#             back against one pid, the second exited 5.
#
#             Leave roughly a minute between runs on one pid, and give CI its
#             own.
#
# Note that Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes
# a bare host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer
# authenticate on the WebSocket upgrade and work. selenium_scraper.py refuses
# a credentialed endpoint with exit 2 and says which engine to use instead.
#
# One more thing to expect: a credential here does not last. Every endpoint
# inherited from this family's sibling repos was already returning 401
# `deny_no_user` when this repo was written, which is why the canary workflow
# is dispatch-only rather than nightly.
TOKOPEDIA_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-id-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222

# --- Proxy ----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT CURRENTLY USABLE FROM A BROWSER ON THIS SITE, and that is unexplained
# rather than excused.
#
# Measured 2026-09-10: the 2Captcha residential gateway does reach a real
# Indonesian exit — 36.77.157.93, Bandung, Telkom Indonesia — and plain
# `requests` fetches through it fine. But EVERY Chromium navigation through
# it timed out, including shopee.co.id as a control, so it is the
# browser-plus-proxy combination rather than anything to do with Tokopedia.
# Until that is understood, use TOKOPEDIA_CDP_ENDPOINT above.
#
# The flag is wired and correct if you have a proxy that works: one URL here,
# or --proxy-file with one per line for a pool. A pool is what spreads a
# run's volume, and --concurrency without one just sends N times the traffic
# from a single address.
#
# The credentials here never reach the browser's command line — they go
# through the driver's own fields. Logs keep the host and port and mask the
# rest, because which exit a run used is the point of the log and is not the
# secret. Selenium's --proxy-server cannot authenticate at all, so that
# engine strips the credentials and warns rather than letting you believe a
# user:pass URL is doing something.
TOKOPEDIA_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@ap.proxy.2captcha.com:2334

# --- Default target -------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. Tokopedia is ONE storefront with one language and one
# currency, so there is no locale prefix and no per-country hostname to get
# wrong.
#
# Which URL you pick decides more than the products, because the two listing
# kinds behave differently:
#
#   /p/<cat>/<sub>[/<subsub>]   a category listing. Paginates with ?page=N,
#                               60 products per page, and --concurrency works.
#   /search?st=product&q=...    a search grid. ONE infinitely scrolling page:
#                               ?page=2 on a search URL returns an EMPTY
#                               result set rather than page 2, so --pages
#                               above 1 is honoured by scrolling further, and
#                               --concurrency is refused with that reason.
#   /p/<slug>                   a DISCOVERY HUB with no product grid on it.
#                               Answers 200 and yields zero rows, which is
#                               exit 4 and not a fault.
#   /{shop}/{slug}              one product, with --mode product.
TOKOPEDIA_URL=https://www.tokopedia.com/p/makanan-minuman/minuman/kopi-bubuk

# Deliberately NOT here: an output prefix. `--out` already carries a
# non-empty default, so the loader — which only fills UNSET values — would
# never see it, and the variable would be silently inert: a setting that
# looks configurable and is not.
